source: tests/fast_suite/ui/errors/mod.rs
---
  ✕ `#[equality]` conflicts with a specialized `equals`
   ╭─[test.lis:2:1]
 1 │ 
 2 │ #[equality]
   · ─────┬─────
   ·      ╰── would synthesize an `equals` of its own
 3 │ struct Pair<A, B> { a: A, b: B }
   ╰────
  help: Write `equals` as a plain `fn equals(self, other: Self) -> bool` over the whole type, or remove `#[equality]`. An `equals` over a partial or concrete receiver (`impl Box<int>`, `impl<T> Pair<T, T>`), or one with extra type parameters (`fn equals<U>`, `impl<T, U> Box<T>`), is emitted as a free function and cannot satisfy `#[equality]` · code: [attribute.equality_specialized_equals]
